The main cost here is the `std::string` copy on return. The original ternary builds an extra temporary from `""` and then copies `units` into it, so the version below returns `units` directly through the return slot. The observable behavior is unchanged, but the gain is modest because the copy itself remains.

```cpp
std::string FieldBase::GetUnits(const FIT_UINT16 subFieldIndex) const
{
    if (subFieldIndex >= GetNumSubFields())
        return GetUnits();

    const auto subfield = GetSubField(subFieldIndex);
    if (NULL != subfield)
        return subfield->units;
    return std::string();
}
```